https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k_0U3DlLFSU  (Capo 0) (MC0)

TIP:  For the intro, form (Am) and pick the 5th string and then the 6th before strumming the first (Am).  Thump-thump-strum.

TIP:  (Cmaj7) is just (C) without the index finger on the lower string <c>.

TIP:  To play the (E) (Esus) (E) (Am) sequence keep the (E) shape and simply add your pinky to the 3rd string/2nd fret <a> and then remove it - on/off - and then move to the (Am).  Easy.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)

TIP:  There’s a little riff in the chorus indicated by the (F) x 7 - (G) and (C) x 4 - (G) x 4 - (C) and that's exactly what you do, strum (F) (C) or (G) quickly the number of times indicated.
 
       
